{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He passed.</b> Do not wonder that HaShem calls the Name, for He alone knows and knowledge and known, and this is a matter very deep. The Gaon [Saadia] said that the first Name is joined with ויקרא, but if so why did the master of the accents not join it? The correct view is that the Name is twice, like אברהם אברהם, יעקב יעקב, משה משה — so it is read and written, for they are thirteen attributes. The Gaon said that the revered Name, by count — if so it is not an attribute; and secondly, that it is 'Adonai' — and this is an error, for what is written is not 'Adonai' but rather it is a reverent appellation according to the speaker, in the way of honor. Rabbi Nissim said that the word ארך אפים is two attributes — for the righteous and for the wicked — this too is not correct, for an attribute is not multiplied because of a change in the person; and furthermore, HaShem is ארך אפים to the wicked, and not to those who did not sin. And behold, ונקה is an attribute on its own — thus far, thirteen attributes, by way of peshat. ונקה לא ינקה is one attribute, for ונקה is a verb form, like אם ענה תענה אותו (Exodus 22:22); rather we learn from the word ונקה לא ינקה that for those who turn back He does not acquit, but for those who return He acquits, as the words of the prophets — therefore the word ונקה was included in the count of attributes. <b>And the word פקד עון אבות.</b> It too is an attribute of mercy. Know that the priestly garments are seven, and because the tzitz is like an ornament it was included in the count, and behold they are eleven. And eleven tribes were born in Paddan-aram, and Benjamin alone was born in the land of Canaan; and it is written of all of them: אלה בני יעקב אשר יולד לו בפדן ארם (Genesis 35:26), for it followed the majority and did not scruple to remove the one. And likewise: בשבעים נפש ירדו אבותיך מצרימה (Deuteronomy 10:22) — and Manasseh and Ephraim did not go down, for there they were born. And behold, the revered Name — they included it among the attributes; it is a noun of essence, and I have already mentioned in the portion ואלה שמות that sometimes it is an adjective and sometimes an attribute, and they are two:" "<b>And the word El.</b> Third:" "<b>Compassionate.</b> Fourth:" "<b>And gracious.</b> Fifth:" "<b>Slow to anger.</b> Sixth:" "<b>And abundant in kindness.</b> Seventh:" "<b>And the word 'abundant.'</b> It serves in relation to another: ורב <b>truth.</b> Eighth:" "<b>Preserving kindness for thousands.</b> Ninth:" "<b>Bearing iniquity.</b> Tenth:" "And bearing <b>transgression.</b> Eleventh:" "And bearing <b>sin.</b> Twelfth:" "<b>And acquitting.</b> Thirteenth:" "And the Name, which is a comprehensive epithet — the revered and the lowly, the exalted and the humble:" "<b>And El.</b> Like 'mighty,' who does what is proper in wisdom:" "<b>And compassionate.</b> In the manner of כרחם אב על בנים (Psalms 103:13) — that He guards them lest they fall:" "<b>And gracious.</b> In the manner of כי חנון אני (Exodus 22:26) — to save one who has fallen and cannot rise:" "<b>Slow to anger.</b> That He is not quickly angered at the wicked:" "<b>And abundant in kindness.</b> To the righteous and to the wicked:" "<b>And abundant in truth.</b> That He fulfills and upholds His word:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The passage about the priestly garments and the eleven tribes is textually difficult; it appears to be a digression or may be corrupt. Translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:25.740889458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}